      {
        "id": 28990,
        "name": "lugaru",
        "username": "lugaru",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lugaru/{size}/2767_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-04-26T17:20:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You should go back and read all those old issues with Daredevil struggling with The Kingpin… or the new Punisher Max (by Jason Aaron) with similar themes (if you are 18 years or older, it is a very nasty book in a good way). Chairman/Operative are really evocative of those characters, which is a hard feat to pull off.</p>\n<p>Now for a really old movie that you would dig along these lines, check out Branded to Kill. It was a huge influence on my tastes, it is a japanese gangster film that starts out with hitmen and eventually branches into straight up psychedelic arthouse madness.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:02:56.341Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
